      "message": "Drive-by, without changing logic here, switching to the kDst primitive blend mode in the draw-shadow code won\u0027t help collapse the pipeline as much as we could. We were seeing a hard-coded kModulate before because it\u0027s not a Porter-duff coefficient blend. kDst is, so we\u0027d end up with a fairly general purpose pipeline being compiled.\n\nHowever, what would be ideal is that if we see that it\u0027s kDst and `fSkipColorXform` is true, we treat it as a fixed kDst and skip even calling `this-\u003eaddPaintColorToKey()` because the blend mode would erase anything that branch computed.",
